        "original_id": "07b3b296-1c9e-5cac-b664-0c1700e444bc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: America Is Dying Slowly, Breakadawn, Buhloone Mindstate\n- Organizations: Red Hot Organization\n- People: De La Soul, Mobb Deep, Coolio, Biz Markie, Chubb Rock, The Lost Boyz, Pete Rock, Common, Wu-Tang Clan\n- Places: Long Island, New York\n- Concepts: AIDS, Red Hot AIDS Benefit Series\n\nFacts:\n- De La Soul is an American hip hop trio that was formed in 1987 on Long Island, New York.\n- \"Breakadawn\" is a 1993 single by De La Soul from the group's third album, \"Buhloone Mindstate.\"\n- America Is Dying Slowly is a compilation album whose title is a backronym for AIDS.\n- America Is Dying Slowly is the eighth entry in the Red Hot AIDS Benefit Series recorded by the Red Hot Organization.\n- America Is Dying Slowly featured collaborations from hip hop acts including Mobb Deep, De La Soul, Coolio, Biz Markie, Chubb Rock, The Lost Boyz, Pete Rock, Common, and Wu-Tang Clan.",
